From 3d9719aa8b78ab4dc6a1a9767f8050bfda320d36 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joachim Wiberg <troglobit@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 11:13:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] port-probe: trust the ID_MM_PORT_TYPE_MBIM udev tag
Organization: Wires

When a udev rule explicitly sets ID_MM_PORT_TYPE_MBIM=1 on a port,
treat it as definitive and skip the active MBIM probe.  This mirrors
how ID_MM_PORT_TYPE_GPS is handled.  Ports that are only guessed to be
MBIM, from their driver or wwan port type, are still probed.

The active MBIM probe opens the WDM device and sends an MBIM OPEN
message.  Some modems, e.g., Dell DW5811e (Sierra Wireless EM7455 in
USB composition 8), keep sending QMI/QMUX framed notifications on the
MBIM control channel before ever answering MBIM OPEN, so the probe
times out after ~50 s.  mm_port_probe_list_has_mbim_port() then
returns FALSE, the Dell plugin creates a non-MBIM modem object, and
the usbmisc port ends up as "unhandled port type".

A udev rule that sets the tag already matches on vendor, product and
interface, so the active probe adds no information for such a port.

Signed-off-by: Joachim Wiberg <troglobit@gmail.com>
---
 src/mm-port-probe.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/mm-port-probe.c b/src/mm-port-probe.c
index 85f30e60..d3be5ed4 100644
--- a/src/mm-port-probe.c
+++ b/src/mm-port-probe.c
@@ -1529,6 +1529,9 @@ mm_port_probe_run (MMPortProbe                *self,
     /* If this is a port flagged as being a MBIM port, don't do any other probing */
     if (self->priv->maybe_mbim) {
         mm_obj_dbg (self, "no AT/QCDM/QMI probing in possible MBIM port");
+        /* An explicit udev tag is definitive, skip the MBIM probe too */
+        if (mm_kernel_device_get_property_as_boolean (self->priv->port, ID_MM_PORT_TYPE_MBIM))
+            mm_port_probe_set_result_mbim (self, TRUE);
         mm_port_probe_set_result_at   (self, FALSE);
         mm_port_probe_set_result_qcdm (self, FALSE);
         mm_port_probe_set_result_qmi  (self, FALSE);
